    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2PEr8d8qm8VxeVuDCKmZ2zK)_\n\n## What\nTwo commits.\n\n1. **Fix**: `sp-split--denote-rename` passed 5 arguments to `denote-rename-file`, but the installed Denote takes 4 (no DATE). It now passes only as many optional arguments as `func-arity` says the installed version accepts.\n2. **Tag menu**: `sp-org-tag-groups-read-tags` is a completion menu with tags headed and sorted by `sp-org-tag-groups-alist` group, each annotated with its group chip. `sp-org-tag-read-note-tags` (used by note creation and wikilink conversion) uses it when `sp-org-tag-groups` is loaded. `sp-split-leave-parents` asks for tags when the split note has none (`sp-split-ask-tags`), writes `#+filetags`, and Denote names the file from them (Denote casing is unchanged).\n\n## Not tested\nNo Emacs in the container. I could not check the installed Denote's signature directly, so the arity is inferred from the error. Unregistered tags still go through the existing register prompt.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA2qUy6iDGHnuKJjyb)_",
